# Third-party software in Actinium

Actinium's own code is MIT licensed. The jar also contains the following.

## VulkanMod

- **Version:** 0.6.7 for Minecraft 1.21.1, ported from Fabric to NeoForge
- **Source in this repository:** `src/main/java/net/vulkanmod`, `src/main/resources/assets/vulkanmod`
- **Licence:** LGPL-3.0, full text in [`LICENSE-VulkanMod-LGPL-3.0.txt`](LICENSE-VulkanMod-LGPL-3.0.txt)
- **Author:** Collateral, https://github.com/xCollateral/VulkanMod

This is the Vulkan renderer. It is compiled into Actinium rather than shipped as a separate mod,
and it has been modified: the Fabric entry point, Fabric Rendering API hooks and fluid rendering
are replaced with their NeoForge equivalents, NeoForge's model data and render stage events are
wired in, and several defects are fixed. The modified files stay under LGPL-3.0.

LGPL-3.0 requires that you can rebuild Actinium against your own changes to the renderer. The
complete source is in this repository and `./gradlew build` produces the jar.

## Fabric Rendering API interfaces

- **Source in this repository:** `src/main/java/net/vulkanmod/render/chunk/build/frapi/api`
- **Licence:** Apache-2.0
- **Author:** FabricMC, https://github.com/FabricMC/fabric

The interfaces VulkanMod's chunk builder is written against, relocated into the renderer's own
package so they cannot clash with a Fabric API port installed alongside.

## LWJGL (Vulkan, VMA, shaderc bindings)

- **Shipped at:** `META-INF/jarjar/lwjgl-{vulkan,vma,shaderc}-3.3.3*.jar`, unmodified apart from
  a manifest entry that tells NeoForge to load them as libraries
- **Licence:** BSD-3-Clause, https://www.lwjgl.org/license
